id: pm-eugaqy
title: "The canonical spelling the output contract tells agents to adopt returns every row with every field stripped, and only the one surface that validates its selectors refuses it"
description: "The universal read-output layer folds two unrelated kinds of legacy flag into one canonical option. Value-bearing aliases (--fields, --section) name row fields. Mode aliases (--brief, --compact, --full, --summary, --counts, --collapse) name a whole declared projection. Both are mapped to a bare token by flagSelector(), both are advertised through the same emitted migration hint, and only the first kind was ever implemented.\n\napplyIncludeProjection treats every canonical token as a field name. A mode token matches no field, so projectRecordFields returns an empty object for every row. The envelope is not corrected: projection.fields still declares the field list that was removed, count still reports the row count, and the process exits 0.\n\nMeasured at HEAD build 2026.8.13, over the 18 (surface, declared mode) pairs reachable from the contract table:\n\n  surface     modes probed   rows emptied   exit\n  list        3              5 of 5         0\n  search      2              5 of 5         0\n  contracts   2              131 of 131     0\n  validate    1              9 of 9         0\n  history     1              5 of 5         0\n  activity    1              5 of 5         0\n  get         1              none           2\n\n10 of 18 pairs return the requested row count as empty objects. The single surface that refuses is get, because applyGetIncludeProjection enumerates its legal selectors and throws; every other surface has no enumeration and therefore no refusal.\n\nTwo properties make this worse than an ordinary projection bug.\n\nThe tool recommends the broken spelling itself. The receipt on a legacy invocation emits 'compatibility alias; prefer --output-include brief'. An agent that follows the hint the tool just printed receives rows with no content and no error. The hint is asserted in tests/fixtures/contracts/full.json as a string and executed nowhere, so the recommendation was frozen while the behaviour behind it never existed.\n\nThe affected surfaces include the orientation path. pm contracts is where AGENTS.md routes an agent to discover exact flag contracts; --output-include full empties all 131 rows of it. pm validate --output-include counts empties the governance counts. A caller cannot distinguish this from a workspace that holds nothing.\n\nThe root cause is ordering, not vocabulary: a projection mode selects which fields the command computes, so it can only be honoured before the command runs, while the output layer runs after. Mode tokens have to be handed back to the command that owns them."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",contracts,output-contract,regression,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-13T21:09:07.273Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T21:26:21.620Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-13T21:19:20.438Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-13T21:19:20.438Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Every include-dimension migration hint that recommends a bare token resolves that token to the projection mode its legacy alias owns, on every read surface that declares it; A canonical include request is byte-identical to the legacy alias it replaces for all 16 declared (surface, mode) pairs, excluding only the receipt that records which spelling was used; A selector that matches no field on any returned row is refused with the exit code and legal domain the get surface already uses, instead of returning rows with no fields and exit 0; A test executes every emitted migration hint rather than pinning its text, so a recommendation that stops working fails CI; The MCP action path and the CLI path resolve a mode token identically"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Split the canonical include dimension into declared projection modes and residual field selectors; modes are forwarded to the owning command before it computes rows, and an all-empty projection is refused with the surface's legal domain."
expected_result: "pm list --output-include brief returns the same rows as pm list --brief, and an unrecognised selector is refused."
actual_result: "All 16 declared (surface, mode) pairs are byte-identical to their legacy flag; unrecognised selectors exit 2 naming the declared modes; full suite green at 7,272 tests."
